  "Number": 11,
  "Question": "The solution of the equation \\(7^{x+7}=8^x\\) can be expressed in the form \\(x=\\log_b 7^7.\\) What is \\(b?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{15}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{8}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{8}{7}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{15}{8}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{15}{7}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "To identify the logarithm's base, rewrite the equation with a single quantity raised to \\(x\\). Since \\(7^x>0\\), division by \\(7^x\\) is valid and gives\n\\[\n7^7=\\frac{8^x}{7^x}=\\left(\\frac87\\right)^x.\n\\]\nBy definition, \\(a^x=N\\) is equivalent to \\(x=\\log_a N\\) when \\(a>0\\), \\(a\\ne1\\), and \\(N>0\\). Here these conditions hold, so\n\\[\nx=\\log_{8/7}(7^7).\n\\]\nThus \\(\\boxed{b=\\frac87}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
